SUMMARY:[WEATHER WATCH] OFFICIAL NWS ALERT — Heat Advisory
DESCRIPTION:Location: Itasca\, IL\n\nHeat Advisory issued September 3 at 1:08AM CDT until September 3 at 7:00PM CDT by NWS Chicago IL\n\n* WHAT...Heat index values of 100 to 105 expected. This is the third\nday in a row with forecast or observed heat indices above 100\ndegrees.\n\n* WHERE...Boone\, DuPage\, Kane\, and McHenry Counties.\n\n* WHEN...Until 7 PM CDT this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Hot temperatures and high humidity may cause heat\nillnesses especially after several days of dangerous heat.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...A cold front possibly accompanied by\nthunderstorms will move inland from Lake Michigan this evening\nleading to rapidly improving conditions.
CATEGORIES:Weather Warning
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260903
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260904
END:VEVENT
